    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the frai CLI where the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through to the frai-gate subcommand.\n\n### The Problem\nThe frai CLI uses Commander.js's variadic argument handling `[args...]`, which only captures positional arguments. The `--ci` flag is an option (not positional), so it wasn't included in the `args` array passed to frai-gate, even with `allowUnknownOption(true)` enabled.\n\n### The Solution\nI modified the `gate` command in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to reconstruct all arguments from `process.argv` instead of relying on the variadic `args` parameter. This ensures all flags and options (including `--ci`) are properly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n### What Changed\n**File:** `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755)\n- Extracted all arguments after the `gate` command from `process.argv`\n- Passed the complete argument list to the spawned frai-gate process\n\n### Testing Confirmed\n\u2705 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`  \n\u2705 Tested: `node <repo>/packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci`  \n\u2705 Both files now created:\n  - FRAI-SPEC.md\n  - .github/workflows/rai-gate.yml",
